** TODO A multibyte separator in a narrow facet comes back as its first byte

A narrow =numpunct= or =moneypunct= separator wider than one byte is
returned as its first byte: under =fr_FR.UTF-8= =num_put<char>= writes
"1\xE2234\xE2567", invalid UTF-8; =fr_CA='s money separator is 0xC2.
=22.locale.numpunct= pins the first-byte reading. 14882:2003 makes the
separator one =char=. Found by probe, 2026-11-02.

