third level is ~forward,position~ and both elements are =IGNORE=
there. Seen while the undefined-character check was written,
2026-11-04; the check does not pin it. Hypothesis: the position
level weighs an =IGNORE=d element by its ordinal in the order, or
the database writes a weight for it that is not =<a>='s.

Fix: establish which with =util/locale= on the database, then
either the writer or the position level of =__rw_process_offsets=.

Check: the pair compares 0 on both facets, with a row in
=22.locale.collate=.

