** TODO =operator_delete= reads the header before any pointer it is given

The in-hand check reads 48 bytes before the pointer before it knows
the pointer is a live block. On a freed block that is a read of
freed memory: harmless under glibc for =0.new='s double delete
(=self_= reads as the fill), a fault for an =mmap=-served block that
=malloc= has unmapped (none in the suite), and a heap-use-after-free
report under AddressSanitizer, where the old walk never touched freed
memory. Hypothesis, 2026-11-05.

