** TODO =doc/stdlibref= describes locale behaviour the library does not have

The import's reference pages still document additions that left the
tree, and one that never was:

- =num-get.html= 232: "Input in base 1 through 36 is accepted. Base of
  1 accepts Roman numerals", and =ios_base::bin=. 14882:2003
  22.2.2.1.2, p4 (Table 55) has =oct=, =hex=, an empty =basefield= and
  decimal; 8b5d90ae removed the other bases and =bin= and did not
  touch the page.
- =num-put.html= 295 (the =other(*)= row), 307 ("Output in base 1
  (roman numerals ...) and base 2 through 36"), 392 (the binary digit
  legend) and 441. 22.2.2.2.2, p7 (Table 57); the same commit.
  9a5a402a edited this page for the negative precision and left these.
- =collate.html= 194, 203 and 211: "As an extension of this
  implementation, the =collate<char>= and =collate_byname<char>=
  facets recognize and correctly interpret sequences of multi-byte
  characters." =collate<char>= compares with =memcmp=
  (=src/collate.cpp= 771-787), the lexicographical comparison of
  22.2.4.1.2, p1; for =collate_byname<char>= a multibyte collation is
  the named locale's semantics (22.1.1.1.2, p4), so no extension
  either way.
- =time-get.html= 326: =do_get_year= takes [69,99] as 1969-1999 and
  [0,68] as 2000-2068. The library's =do_get_year= is =%Y=
  (=include/loc/_time_get.h= 160-164): "26" is the year 26
  (=ref-locale.md= 12.3, "Two-digit years in =do_get_year=").
  22.2.5.1.2, p8 makes the choice implementation-defined; the page
  states the other one, the pivot of =%y=.
- =time-put.html= 284-286 and 454: a =%i=, "Hour of the 12-hour day
  [1,12]. Single digits preceded by a blank", marked an extension to
  POSIX. =src/time_put.cpp= has no =i= case; it writes that hour for
  =%l= (1303, 2274), which the page does not list.
- =money-get.html= 178: after the decimal point "optionally, by
  additional digits", the value "multiplied by 10 to the power of" and
  truncated. 22.2.6.3, p3: "The number of digits required after the
  decimal point (if any) is exactly the value returned by
  frac_digits()". 60c683eb made the facet exact (=ref-locale.md=
  10.3.9) and did not touch the page.

No test reads the pages. Found by the extension sweep's reading,
2026-11-04.

Fix: the passages go and =time-put.html='s table gains =%l=; 9a5a402a
set the rule that a removal edits its page.

